{
  "id": "m4l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Métodos de texto",
    "en": "String methods"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Las cadenas tienen superpoderes"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Una cadena (`str`) trae muchos métodos para transformar y consultar texto. No modifican la original (son **inmutables**): devuelven una **nueva** cadena."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "s = \"  Hola Mundo  \"",
          "print(s.strip())",
          "print(s.lower())",
          "print(s.upper())"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Hola Mundo",
          "  hola mundo  ",
          "  HOLA MUNDO  "
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`strip()` quita espacios de los extremos; `lower()`/`upper()` cambian mayúsculas; `replace(a, b)` sustituye; `title()` pone iniciales en mayúscula."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "print(\"ana,bea,sol\".replace(\",\", \" y \"))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "ana y bea y sol"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Buscar y partir"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`'x' in texto` indica si aparece. `find(sub)` da la posición (o -1). `split(sep)` parte en una lista, y `sep.join(lista)` une una lista en una cadena."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "partes = \"a,b,c\".split(\",\")",
          "print(partes)",
          "print(\"-\".join(partes))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "['a', 'b', 'c']",
          "a-b-c"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Como devuelven copias, puedes **encadenar**: `texto.strip().lower().replace(' ', '_')`."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Strings have superpowers"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A string (`str`) comes with many methods to transform and query text. They never change the original (strings are **immutable**): they return a **new** string."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "s = \"  Hola Mundo  \"",
          "print(s.strip())",
          "print(s.lower())",
          "print(s.upper())"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Hola Mundo",
          "  hola mundo  ",
          "  HOLA MUNDO  "
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`strip()` removes edge whitespace; `lower()`/`upper()` change case; `replace(a, b)` substitutes; `title()` capitalises each word."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "print(\"ana,bea,sol\".replace(\",\", \" y \"))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "ana y bea y sol"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Searching and splitting"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`'x' in text` tells if it appears. `find(sub)` gives the position (or -1). `split(sep)` splits into a list, and `sep.join(list)` joins a list into a string."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "partes = \"a,b,c\".split(\",\")",
          "print(partes)",
          "print(\"-\".join(partes))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "['a', 'b', 'c']",
          "a-b-c"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Since they return copies, you can **chain** them: `text.strip().lower().replace(' ', '_')`."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m4l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `normaliza(texto)` que devuelva el texto **sin espacios** al inicio/fin y en **minúsculas**.",
        "en": "Define `normaliza(texto)` returning the text **without** leading/trailing spaces and in **lowercase**."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def normaliza(texto):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def normaliza(texto):",
        "    return texto.strip().lower()"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Encadena strip() y lower().",
          "return texto.strip().lower()"
        ],
        "en": [
          "Chain strip() and lower().",
          "return texto.strip().lower()"
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "normaliza",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                "  Hola "
              ],
              "expected": "hola"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "PYTHON"
              ],
              "expected": "python"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "  a B c "
              ],
              "expected": "a b c"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m4l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `iniciales(nombre)` que devuelva las iniciales en mayúscula. Ej: `'ana perez lopez'` → `'APL'`.",
        "en": "Define `iniciales(nombre)` returning the uppercase initials. E.g. `'ana perez lopez'` → `'APL'`."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def iniciales(nombre):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def iniciales(nombre):",
        "    return \"\".join(p[0].upper() for p in nombre.split())"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "nombre.split() separa por espacios.",
          "Toma p[0] de cada palabra y únelos."
        ],
        "en": [
          "nombre.split() splits on spaces.",
          "Take p[0] of each word and join them."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "iniciales",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                "ana perez lopez"
              ],
              "expected": "APL"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "juan"
              ],
              "expected": "J"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "  maria jose  "
              ],
              "expected": "MJ"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}